  <h2>About Dr. Halvorson</h2>
  <p>
    Dr. Lori Halvorson established <strong>The DUET Method<sup class="tm">&trade;</sup></strong>, an innovative audiology approach focused on neural efficiency and auditory processing. With over 25 years of clinical experience, she has pioneered a comprehensive, prevention-first model of hearing care that strengthens the auditory neural pathways that power memory, focus, and lifelong cognitive health.
  </p>
  <p>
    Her methodology emphasizes <strong>Ear to Brain Fitness<sup class="tm">&trade;</sup></strong>, treating hearing as a brain-driven process rather than an isolated ear condition. Dr. Halvorson's work is influenced by Dr. Nina Kraus's research on rhythm and timing in auditory development, and she leads clinical and humanitarian missions that bring this evidence-based care to underserved communities around the world.
  </p>

  <h2>Credentials</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>AuD — Doctor of Audiology</li>
    <li>FAAA — Fellow, American Academy of Audiology</li>
    <li>ABAC — American Board of Audiology Certified</li>
    <li>CH-TM — Certificate Holder, Tinnitus Management</li>
    <li>Adjunct Lecturer, Northwestern University</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Philosophy</h2>
  <blockquote>
    "Hearing keeps people safe, connected, and cognitively sharp. We are not just treating ears, we are growing brains."
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Areas of Focus</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Diagnostic auditory evaluation and neural processing assessment</li>
    <li>DUET Method<sup class="tm">&trade;</sup> hearing fitness programs</li>
    <li>Tinnitus management</li>
    <li>Hearing preservation for musicians and high-noise professionals</li>
    <li>Global humanitarian hearing missions</li>
  </ul>
